# Start: the system carousel of a REBOOTED VM (awake, nothing open). End:
# USER INTERFACE SETTINGS with its last row -- SHOW RETROACHIEVEMENTS ICON, a
# Settings-backed switch -- toggled and focused. The next B (`z`) closes the
# page and runs GuiSettings::save(): Settings::saveFile() writes
# es_settings.cfg and SystemConf::saveSystemConf() writes system.cfg. KILL13
# (tools/cloud-round-trip) sends that B itself, on the same monitor
# connection as the system_reset that follows it; the harness drops every
# step from the last `key x` on for the walk that changes nothing.
#
# MAIN MENU on ROCKNIX: GAME SETTINGS, CONTROLLER & BLUETOOTH SETTINGS, USER
# INTERFACE SETTINGS, ... -- so START, down, down, A. The page opens on its
# first row (THEME SET); up lands on BACK, up again wraps to the last row.
# On ROCKNIX that is SHOW RETROACHIEVEMENTS ICON: the gun/wheel/trackball/
# spinner rows after it are `#if !defined(ROCKNIX)` (GuiMenu.cpp).
key shift
wait 1
key ret
wait 2
key down
wait 1
key down
wait 1
key x
wait 2
key up
wait 1
key up
wait 1
shot ui-settings-last-row
key x
wait 1
shot toggled
